  "description": "LUYDEP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H103 N6 Nd3 O23 S8,2.5(C3 H7 N1 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 7 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2D (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2E (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 0.624-5.092 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 8.58-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H103N6Nd3O23S8·2.5(dmf).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
